{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"reflective-sticky-grouper","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nCut the next minor release, 0.11.0, from reviewed main using docs/releasing.md. The current package and latest tag are 0.10.1/v0.10.1. PyPI is immutable; publication must use the dispatch-from-main workflow and its required pypi environment approval.\n\n## Plan\n- Work in a fresh worktree based on current origin/main and confirm release prerequisites, identity, recent Gerrit history/rights, and channel state.\n- Bump pyproject.toml and every version in server.json to 0.11.0; generate and hand-curate the 0.11.0 CHANGELOG section and compare links.\n- Run version-lockstep and proportional release preflight: lint, typecheck, full tests, build/twine checks, and release-specific tests/guards.\n- Commit with DCO, Change-Id, and rebar-ticket trailer; send through Gerrit and wait for LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with no unresolved comments, then Submit.\n- After the bump lands on main, dispatch release.yml from main with version=0.11.0 and obtain the required pypi environment approval; monitor the entire workflow to a terminal result.\n- Verify PyPI 0.11.0 plus PEP 740 provenance, the v0.11.0 GitHub tag/release and artifacts, MCP Registry 0.11.0, and the Homebrew tap bump (trigger autobump if useful).\n- Install nava-rebar[mcp]==0.11.0 from PyPI in the distribution-channel environment and run the packaged post-publication probe.\n- Record receipts and results on this ticket, then close it only after all acceptance criteria are met.\n\n## File impact\n- pyproject.toml — package version bump\n- server.json — MCP manifest/package version bump\n- CHANGELOG.md — curated 0.11.0 release notes and compare links\n\n## Rollback / failure policy\nBefore publish, stop on any failed guard, review, or CI vote and remediate through a new Gerrit patchset. After publish, PyPI cannot be replaced: if the artifact is bad, yank 0.11.0, de-list its GitHub Release, and cut a fixed patch version; do not overwrite artifacts or retag published content.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] pyproject.toml, server.json top-level version, every server.json package version, and the dispatch input all equal 0.11.0.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md contains a hand-curated 0.11.0 section dated 2026-08-06, a fresh Unreleased section, and correct compare links.\n- [ ] Local release preflight passes: version-lockstep, release-specific tests/guards, lint, typecheck, full tests, build, and twine artifact checks.\n- [ ] The release bump lands on main through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, no unresolved comments, DCO, Change-Id, and rebar-ticket provenance.\n- [ ] release.yml is dispatched from main for 0.11.0, receives required pypi environment approval, and all required jobs complete successfully.\n- [ ] PyPI serves nava-rebar 0.11.0 and artifact provenance verification succeeds.\n- [ ] GitHub exposes v0.11.0 at the released main SHA with the release marked Latest and wheel/sdist attached.\n- [ ] MCP Registry reports io.github.navapbc/rebar version 0.11.0.\n- [ ] Homebrew tap Formula/rebar.rb points to the 0.11.0 PyPI sdist with the matching SHA-256.\n- [ ] A fresh channel install of nava-rebar[mcp]==0.11.0 passes scripts/probe_rebar.py with zero failures.\n- [ ] Release receipts, any exceptions, and the rollback disposition are recorded on this ticket.","id":"9874-b1a9-2ff1-4cd3","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["release"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Cut rebar 0.11.0 minor release"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786054918370415001,"uuid":"66c84989-a550-4e63-8e7a-0fea74224ed4"}